WHAT THIS LICENCE COVERS

The grant above covers the author's own work in this repository: the KQL
queries, and the prose written around them. "Software" is read to include
both, because the queries and the documentation are interleaved inside the
same markdown files and a boundary drawn between them would have to be
adjudicated fence by fence.

WHAT THIS LICENCE DOES NOT COVER

This repository quotes Microsoft Learn documentation extensively and cites
MITRE and OWASP identifiers. None of the following is the author's to license,
and none of it is relicensed by the grant above:

  - Quoted Microsoft Learn text, including the table, column and value
    descriptions reproduced verbatim in the detection files.
  - Microsoft product names, table names, column names, alert names and alert
    identifiers.
  - MITRE ATLAS technique identifiers and titles.
  - OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications item identifiers and titles.

Every one of those is cited to the source it came from, with the date that
source was read. Those citations sit in the Sources sections of the
detection files and of the cross-walk; the files that repeat the material rely
on them rather than carrying a second copy, so the URL and the date for any
quoted item are in the file that establishes it. Reuse of that material is
governed by its own publisher's terms and not by this file. Read the terms that
apply to the source it was taken from rather than inheriting an assumption from
here.

Microsoft's documentation is not published under a single set of terms, and
which terms reach a given quotation depends on where it was taken from. The
Licence section of README.md records what was established about that, naming
each documentation repository, the licence file in it, and the date that file
was read. It is recorded there so that you know there is a question to answer;
it is not an answer, and nothing in this repository is legal advice.
